# Beneesse project principles

Before planning or implementing any change, read and follow the documentation in `docs/`:

- [docs/index.md](../../docs/index.md) — overview and non-negotiables
- [docs/principles/architecture.md](../../docs/principles/architecture.md) — monorepo layout and dependency rules
- [docs/principles/clean-architecture.md](../../docs/principles/clean-architecture.md) — feature/core layout, BLoC rules, layer flow
- [docs/principles/testing.md](../../docs/principles/testing.md) — coverage targets and test guidance
- [docs/principles/code-quality.md](../../docs/principles/code-quality.md) — Dart/Flutter standards
- [docs/principles/git-and-workflow.md](../../docs/principles/git-and-workflow.md) — commits and PRs
- [docs/principles/tooling.md](../../docs/principles/tooling.md) — FVM, Melos, commands
- [docs/principles/ai-guidelines.md](../../docs/principles/ai-guidelines.md) — AI-specific workflow
- [docs/guides/localization.md](../../docs/guides/localization.md) — ARB keys and adding strings (`beneesse_l10n`)

## Critical rules

1. Use **FVM**: `fvm flutter`, `fvm dart` — not system SDK when versions differ.
2. **`beneesse_api`** is consumed **only** by `beneesse_mobile`. `beneesse_ui` and `beneesse_monitoring` must not depend on it.
3. **Clean Architecture + BLoC** — `flutter_bloc` only; BLoC owns all business logic, orchestration, and display formatting.
4. **Presentation is dumb** — never import repositories, call APIs, or put business/formatting logic in `presentation/` (pages, views, widgets).
5. **Feature layout** — `bloc/`, `presentation/{views,widgets,pages}/`, `data/`, `models/` under `features/<name>/`; shared app code in `core/`.
6. **BLoC → Repository** — no `use_cases` layer; BLoC calls repositories directly.
7. **Coverage** — 100% on workspace packages, app BLoCs, and repositories; app presentation excluded; `beneesse_ui` requires widget + golden tests.
8. **Minimize scope** — smallest correct diff; match existing conventions.
9. Run **`melos run analyze`** before considering work done.
10. Do not commit, push, or amend git history unless the user explicitly asks.
11. Never commit secrets, `.env`, or ignored build/SDK artifacts.

When principles conflict with a user request, ask for clarification rather than violating architecture rules silently.
